WEBVTT

00:00:06.382 --> 00:00:07.842
Thank Paracelsus.

00:00:08.885 --> 00:00:12.347
If you'd have got out,
that could've been quite catastrophic.

00:00:12.931 --> 00:00:15.308
So he's the real reason I came to America.

00:00:19.604 --> 00:00:21.439
To bring Frank home.

00:00:22.482 --> 00:00:23.483
(SCREECHING)

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:24.651
Wait. No, sorry. Stay there.

00:00:24.818 --> 00:00:26.611
-He's a wee bit sensitive to strangers.
-(SCREECHING)

00:00:27.821 --> 00:00:29.823
Here you are. Here you are.

00:00:30.698 --> 00:00:32.242
He was trafficked, you see.

00:00:33.451 --> 00:00:35.745
I found him in Egypt.
He was all chained up.

00:00:36.621 --> 00:00:39.165
Couldn't leave him there.
I had to bring him back.

00:00:39.541 --> 00:00:42.001
I'm gonna put you back
where you belong, aren't I, Frank?

00:00:43.878 --> 00:00:46.381
To the wilds of Arizona.

00:00:47.465 --> 00:00:48.466
(SCREECHES)

00:00:54.848 --> 00:00:55.849
(SCREECHING)

00:01:00.687 --> 00:01:02.480
(CALLING)

00:01:07.569 --> 00:01:09.362
(CREATURES CHITTERING)

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:13.408
(NEWT CONTINUES CALLING)

00:01:22.959 --> 00:01:24.085
(DISTANT RUMBLING)

00:01:24.252 --> 00:01:25.628
All right, here they come.

00:01:26.921 --> 00:01:28.715
Here who comes?

00:01:28.882 --> 00:01:30.091
-Graphorns.
-(WHIMPERS)

00:01:31.092 --> 00:01:32.760
-Hey!
-You're all right.

00:01:35.388 --> 00:01:37.390
-JACOB: Oh!
-Hello.

00:01:37.891 --> 00:01:38.933
Hello.

00:01:40.101 --> 00:01:41.144
(GRAPHORN SNUFFLING)

00:01:41.311 --> 00:01:43.730
So they're the last
breeding pair in existence.

00:01:44.689 --> 00:01:46.524
So if I hadn't managed to rescue them,

00:01:46.691 --> 00:01:49.152
that could've been
the end of Graphorns forever.

00:01:50.695 --> 00:01:51.696
(SNUFFLING)

00:01:54.282 --> 00:01:55.408
All right.

00:02:00.455 --> 00:02:02.332
JACOB: What, you rescue these creatures?

00:02:02.498 --> 00:02:05.335
NEWT: Yes, that's right.
Rescue, nurture and protect them.

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:07.837
And I'm gently trying to educate
my fellow wizards about them.

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:10.506
-(CHIRPS)
-Come on.

00:02:18.222 --> 00:02:19.223
Wow.

00:02:21.935 --> 00:02:23.311
Titus, Finn.

00:02:23.478 --> 00:02:25.271
Poppy, Marlow, Tom.

00:02:26.481 --> 00:02:27.774
(SQUEAKING)

00:02:27.941 --> 00:02:29.651
He had a cold.

00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:31.444
He needed some body warmth.

00:02:31.611 --> 00:02:32.612
JACOB: Aww...

00:02:33.279 --> 00:02:34.656
All right, on you hop.

00:02:34.822 --> 00:02:36.324
(TRILLING)

00:02:36.532 --> 00:02:37.533
(GASPS)

00:02:38.743 --> 00:02:40.203
He has some attachment issues.

00:02:41.287 --> 00:02:42.664
Now, come on, Pickett.

00:02:44.582 --> 00:02:45.583
Pickett.

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:48.503
No, they're not gonna bully you,
now come on.

00:02:49.545 --> 00:02:50.546
Pickett.

00:02:51.506 --> 00:02:52.507
All right.

00:02:54.008 --> 00:02:57.053
And that is exactly why
they accuse me of favoritism.

00:02:58.346 --> 00:02:59.681
Oh, no, Dougal's gone.

00:03:00.556 --> 00:03:03.142
-(CREATURES CHIRPING)
-All right, I'm coming. I'm coming.

00:03:03.518 --> 00:03:05.228
Mum's here. Mum's here.

00:03:05.478 --> 00:03:06.646
Oh, hello.

00:03:07.397 --> 00:03:08.606
Let me take a look at you.

00:03:08.773 --> 00:03:11.359
I know these guys. (CHUCKLES)

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.321
Your Occamy.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:18.157
-What do you mean, my Occamy?
-Yes.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:20.201
Do you want to...

00:03:20.535 --> 00:03:22.912
Oh... Oh, wow, yeah, sure.

00:03:23.079 --> 00:03:24.247
Okay.

00:03:24.497 --> 00:03:26.040
-(WHIMPERS)
-(CHIRPING)

00:03:30.628 --> 00:03:31.713
-Hey.
-(CHIRPS)

00:03:32.213 --> 00:03:33.214
(HISSES)

00:03:33.423 --> 00:03:35.049
-Ahh!
-Oh, sorry, no, don't pet him.

00:03:35.216 --> 00:03:37.552
They, um, learn to
defend themselves early.

00:03:37.719 --> 00:03:40.388
See, their shells are made of silver,
so they're incredibly valuable.

00:03:40.555 --> 00:03:41.597
Okay.

00:03:41.764 --> 00:03:43.933
Their nests tend to get
ransacked by hunters.

00:03:44.183 --> 00:03:45.560
Thank you.

00:03:47.478 --> 00:03:48.563
Mr. Scamander?

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:49.772
Oh, call me Newt.

00:03:50.648 --> 00:03:52.775
Newt. I don't think I'm dreaming.

00:03:53.234 --> 00:03:54.485
What gave it away?

00:03:55.403 --> 00:03:57.321
I ain't got the brains to make this up.

00:04:00.616 --> 00:04:02.243
Would you mind
throwing some of those pellets

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:04.037
in with the Mooncalfs over there?

00:04:06.039 --> 00:04:07.749
-Yeah, sure.
-Just over there's...

00:04:08.916 --> 00:04:09.917
(JACOB CHUCKLES)

00:04:11.461 --> 00:04:12.754
Bugger.

00:04:13.004 --> 00:04:14.505
Niffler's gone.

00:04:14.672 --> 00:04:16.424
Course he has, little bugger.

00:04:16.591 --> 00:04:19.385
Any chance to get his hands
on something shiny.

00:04:28.269 --> 00:04:29.729
(ALL CHITTERING)

00:04:43.618 --> 00:04:45.661
(ROARING)

00:04:50.458 --> 00:04:51.501
(CHIRPING)

00:04:56.547 --> 00:04:58.633
JACOB: What did you do today, Jacob?
(LAUGHS)

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.426
I was inside a suitcase.

00:05:00.593 --> 00:05:01.969
Hey.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:03.638
Oh, hello, fellas.

00:05:03.805 --> 00:05:05.598
-All right. All right.
-(ALL SQUEAKING)

00:05:05.765 --> 00:05:08.434
Take it easy. Take it easy.

00:05:16.275 --> 00:05:17.777
(CHUCKLING) Cutie.

00:05:18.778 --> 00:05:20.488
There it is.

00:05:22.365 --> 00:05:23.950
(WIND WHOOSHING)

